September 19th 2026
I was in the process of setting up my home server but turns out my MacBook was unable to connect to my server.
I had to diagnose it to check whether or not if my Mac was trying to connect to the server for a completely different device

After some diagnostics running commands such as ping and nc, to check if the server actually was up or not, it infact was. However, it appears that the server shared an IP with another device.

As a result I had to configure the hostname and the ip address to something differently simply using the nano terminal and after rebooting it solved the issue.

